      "headline": "Fuel prices at record high due to Middle East war as Lecornu delays then schedules new aid package for June",
      "summary": "Petrol prices in France reached their highest level since the start of the Iran war on 27 February, exceeding €2 per litre for SP95; fiscal revenues from fuel fell sharply as consumption dropped ~30%, undermining a 'windfall' narrative. Prime Minister Lecornu announced he would present a new support package for heavy drivers and affected sectors on Thursday 21 May, after weeks of criticism for slow action."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Book 'Un couple (presque) parfait' reignites Macron marital rumours; Élysée denies",
      "summary": "A new book by Paris Match journalist Florian Tardif claimed that Brigitte Macron's filmed slap of the president during their 2025 Vietnam visit was triggered by a jealous quarrel over messages Macron allegedly exchanged with Franco-Iranian actress Golshifteh Farahani. Both Brigitte Macron's entourage and the Élysée denied the account; the book drove days of tabloid and political media coverage."
    },
    {
      "headline": "Macron's Africa Forward summit in Nairobi yields €23bn investment pledge but raises questions on France's retreat",
      "summary": "President Macron attended the Africa Forward 2026 summit in Nairobi (11–12 May) co-hosted with Kenyan President Ruto, pledging €23 billion in development commitments and acknowledging France had been 'overtaken' by Turkey, China and the US on the continent. The visit included a stop in Ethiopia to meet PM Abiy Ahmed, and prompted commentary on whether France's 'Françafrique' model can be reformed."
